viserys sitting down once again  giving me the same look my grandpa did  when i tried to explain what twerking  was here we have harwin going to town on  sir kristen cole with aegon eamon  jacarys and lucerus watching in the  background with harwin firmly on team  rhaenyra and kristen team allison  something has obviously pissed harwen  off maybe kristen made a snide comment  about rhaenyra or harwin being the  father of her children in the book there  is mention of a brawl occurring after  eamonn calls rhaenyra's sons strongs the  result of this brawl is harwin being  removed as princess rhaenyra's champion  by king viserys maybe this scene is some  sort of adaptation of that and kristen  would obviously be protecting eamonn and  here's viserys in front of that damned  model city as alison tells her husband  to have three children look nothing like  their father it's an insult it seems the  main drive of this episode will be  centered around this rumor that rhaenyra  has been sleeping around with harwin and  that her children are his there are  three random shots that don't give away  too much like renera holding joffrey  alison having a drink after a long day  of trying to destroy her former bestie  and loris who you gotta keep your eyes  on he's always up to no good here's a  shot of someone who kinda looks like  lionel but this dude's got some hair up  top it's not looking good for him and on  the top right we see some guards  approaching looks like this guy might be  getting something chopped off and in  game of thrones that's never a good  thing here we see the aftermath of some  sort of fire or explosion there's a dead  body being carried on a stretcher and  behind them someone with a bucket of  water rushing past for those of you who  have read the book there is one  particularly famous fire that occurs at  harrenhal in which both lionel strong  and harwin are burned alive perhaps this  is that event and there is a brief image  from one of the previous trailers that  shows someone possibly harwin burning in  this fire jacaris takes after his mother  saying the word dracharus ordering his  dragon to roast some goat there seems to  be no shortage of fire this episode and  a lot to look forward to including our  first taste of olivia cook and emma  darcy as alison and raniera if you want  more game of thrones content be sure to  check out my full episode breakdowns  i'll leave links to those in the  description thanks for watching be sure  to like and subscribe and for more bad  takes you can follow me on twitter and  instagram at think story yt until next  time remember so far i'm giving dolores  four peter baelish's out of five
 

